From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:47:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cpu/intel/haswell: Lock the TSEG base before D_LCK

northbridge_final() sets the lock bits of the memory map registers of
the host bridge, TSEGMB among them. On a ThinkPad W541 every one of
them reads back set but that of TSEGMB (0x7f800000): smm_lock() set
D_LCK long before, and with D_LCK the host bridge no longer takes
writes to TSEGMB, the lock bit included (a write of the bit from the
OS does not take either). The base cannot be moved, but the HSTI of the
payload and chipsec's smm_dma read the bit and report the TSEG as not
locked.

Set the bit in smm_lock(), just before D_LCK. Nothing writes the base
after the SMM relocation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Id500722e70d6e32b156d536d33c821ef265be6fb
---
 src/cpu/intel/haswell/smmrelocate.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cpu/intel/haswell/smmrelocate.c b/src/cpu/intel/haswell/smmrelocate.c
index 6ce41965d1..fc88fdfeec 100644
--- a/src/cpu/intel/haswell/smmrelocate.c
+++ b/src/cpu/intel/haswell/smmrelocate.c
@@ -265,5 +265,16 @@ void smm_lock(void)
 	 * make the SMM registers writable again.
 	 */
 	printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "Locking SMM.\n");
+
+	/*
+	 * The lock of the TSEG base first. Once D_LCK is set the host bridge
+	 * no longer takes writes to TSEGMB, its lock bit included: the write
+	 * of northbridge_final(), which comes later, left it clear (read on a
+	 * ThinkPad W541: 0x7f800000 with the other locks of that function set,
+	 * and a write of the bit from the OS does not take either). The base
+	 * cannot move then, but what checks the platform reads the bit (HSTI,
+	 * chipsec smm_dma).
+	 */
+	pci_or_config32(pcidev_on_root(0, 0), TSEG, 1 << 0);
 	pci_write_config8(pcidev_on_root(0, 0), SMRAM, D_LCK | G_SMRAME | C_BASE_SEG);
 }
